# Build output. `make all` stages what the forge would collect under dist/;
# it is a product of the tree, not part of it.
/dist/

# KEY MATERIAL AND SSH CONFIGURATION NEVER ENTER THIS REPOSITORY.
#
# Every key a developer holds is generated inside Vault and reaches them through
# the onboarding bundle -- the workspace key, the bastion key, the forge key --
# and reaches the workspace through Nomad's Vault templates. The sshd
# configuration under .devcontainer/config is the SERVER's contract and carries
# no key. A private key copied into a checkout by hand, or a laptop's
# ~/.ssh/config pasted in for convenience, would be pushed to the forge and
# built into an image, and an image is not un-pushed by deleting the file
# afterwards. So the shapes such files take are refused here, before git sees
# them.
*.key
*.pem
id_*
!id_*.pub
*_rsa
*_ed25519
*_ecdsa
authorized_keys
known_hosts
.ssh/
config.d/
ssh_config
*-workspace-onboarding/
*-workspace-onboarding.tar.gz
*-workspace-onboarding.zip

# Local environment and tokens.
.env
*.env
.envrc
